    <h2 id="defects-heading" class="t-label">defects the suite exposed</h2>
    <ol class="defects">
      <li>
        <h3>A model reply limit was dropped</h3>
        <p>
          One agent setup ignored the configured reply limit. The integration
          was changed to pass the limit through and save it with the run
          settings.
        </p>
        <p class="source">
          Source file: <code>evals-README.md</code> records the correction but
          does not identify the changed implementation file.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>An agent wrote outside its workspace</h3>
        <p>
          Agents attempted writes beyond the task workspace. The suite added
          macOS write confinement, and result notes retain denied paths.
        </p>
        <p class="source">
          Source files: <code>local-model-eval-suite-requirements.md</code>
          describes the isolation boundary;
          <code>playground-results.csv</code> records denied-write notes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>A timed-out request could be retried</h3>
        <p>
          A request that timed out could be retried after cancellation. The
          suite now scores the timeout as a failure and refuses replacement
          requests for that run.
        </p>
        <p class="source">
          Source files: <code>ladder-build.md</code> describes the timeout
          behavior; <code>evals-README.md</code> identifies the fix record.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

